All these deposits are on Borealis (https://borealisdata.ca).

The three 1998 surveys cover francophones only. The codebook of the deposit
says it was decided to keep only francophones ("retenir uniquement les
francophones"); the CROP file kept respondents whose language of use is
French, and the CREATEC file respondents whose mother tongue is French. The
definition used for the combined qes1998 panel file is pending: the deposit
does not state it.


2. The 2022 study (CC BY-NC 4.0): nothing ships
------------------------------------------------

  qes2022             2022 Quebec Election Study. Mahéo, Bélanger,        10.7910/DVN/PAQBDR
                      Stephenson, Harell (Harvard Dataverse)

This study is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). Until its authors agree
in writing, qesR ships none of its value labels, question text or answer
counts.
The package holds only its catalog entry (title, authors, version, file
names, sizes and checksums, as published on the deposit), the names of the
variables that get_qes_master() and get_decon() read
(inst/extdata/legacy/sources.csv), rules written for qesR that say which
codes mark item nonresponse (inst/extdata/dict/shard_rules.csv), and the
rows of the harmonization spec (inst/extdata/harmonize/): variable names,
codes, the md5 hash of each normalized value label (used to check that the
labels of your copy are the ones the spec was written for, without shipping
them), page references to its codebook, and the facts about its waves and
weights that the codebook publishes (pp. 5 and 7): the size of each wave,
its fieldwork dates and mode, and the weighting method (raking on age,
gender, education and language, the trimming bounds). No count from its
data file ships (gates.csv and expected/marginals.csv have no qes2022
row). expected/hashes.csv holds, for each of its harmonized columns, the
md5 hash of the column that qesR computes from the pinned file (used to
check that the harmonization gives the same result on your copy); a hash
cannot be turned back into answers or counts. Its codebook
is built on your computer from your own copy of the data file. When you use
this study, the licence requires attribution (qes_cite("qes2022")) and rules
out commercial use.


3. Other sources
----------------

  - inst/extdata/catalog/elections.csv: election dates, from the official
    results published by Élections Québec (each row gives its source URL).
  - inst/extdata/legacy/: which variable each column of get_qes_master() and
    get_decon() read in qesR 0.4.4, and the labels 0.4.4 attached by hand;
    part of qesR (MIT).
